# DECSWL (ESC # 5) returns the cursor's line to single width. On the line
# DECDWL made double width, CUF stops at column 5 of 10; after DECSWL the
# cursor stays on its character position, CUF reaches column 10 again, and
# printing wraps after the screen's last column.
# spec: the VT100 User Guide, DECSWL and DECDWL
# capability: decswl
size 10 3
send "\e#6abc\e[99C"
check
want cursor 4,0
send "\e#5"
check
want cursor 4,0
send "\e[99C\e[1;4Hdefghijk"
check
want row 0 |abcdefghij|
want row 1 |k|
